## Start here

1. Read [the masterplan](.backlog/masterplan/MASTERPLAN.md) for current state,
   goals, constraints, roadmap, vocabulary and open questions.
2. Run `backlog instructions overview`, then search and inspect relevant tasks.
3. Before creating, executing or finalizing a task, read the matching Backlog
   guide named by the overview.
4. Keep changes within the approved task. Record unrelated discoveries as
   proposed follow-up work instead of expanding scope silently.

The active Backlog task is the execution-plan record. The masterplan contains
only cross-task state and direction; it does not duplicate task status or
implementation narrative.

